  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Resolved from the overview",
      "items": [
        "API process: the only direct source call from an HTTP route is the connection test (POST …/connection/test → ConnectionService.test → Connector.test).",
        "Model-written SQL comes only from the assistant's run_source_query tool → SourceQueryService.run. It runs where the assistant runs: the app for chat, the worker for assistant_task jobs.",
        "Connector.query has one caller, SourceQueryService (connector.py:203-209)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Guards on model SQL",
      "items": [
        "Owners and editors only; the system needs a live Connection and a Snapshot.",
        "Name-based PII rules must have run on the latest Snapshot.",
        "sqlglot query guard (internal/query_guard.py) parses the SQL; only regenerated SafeQuery.sql is sent.",
        "Statement timeout from the run's remaining budget, row cap 100, PII masking, audit row per query."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Stored state (not drawn as edges)",
      "items": [
        "SourceQueryService and the job services each read the connections row and unseal the password with SecretBox before building ConnectionParams.",
        "Job results go to the sources module's own tables: snapshots, src_tables, src_columns, column_profiles, pii_findings, relationships.",
        "Schema Import (import_service.py) builds Snapshots from uploaded files and never opens a source connection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Uncertain",
      "items": [
        "Relationship inference connects only when params_for_source is set (value-overlap step); its other steps use the Snapshot (relationship_service.py:236-246).",
        "Per-driver read-only enforcement differs by engine (\"where the engine supports it\"); each driver file was not audited."
      ]
    }
  ]
